# Autonomy

Operate autonomously for Deli Matsuo. Do not bounce engineering,
implementation-order, or “should I push?” questions. Commit, push, open PRs
to `delimatsuo/heykevin`, and `gh pr merge --merge` when a slice is
reviewed-clean and not owner-gated.

Full law: `docs/agent-operating.md`.

# Work in a worktree

Never trust the primary checkout (local `main` is often behind). Work in a
git worktree under `<clone>/.worktrees/`, discovered or created from the
current clone. On Deli's Mac the clone is
`/Volumes/Extreme Pro/MYPROJECTS/Kevin` — example only, not a gate.
`git fetch origin main`; cut branches from **origin/main**. Pin the
resolved absolute worktree path in every subagent prompt. One git-mutation
owner per worktree.

# Owner-gated — stop and ask

- Cloud/spend/credentials; production or staging Cloud Run deploy
- Enabling `customer_memory_*`, `service_request_mutations_enabled`,
  `SERVICE_REQUEST_RECOVERY_ENABLED`, `jobber_lead_capture_enabled`,
  `PUBLIC_DEMO_ENABLED`
- App Store / TestFlight; Twilio number buy/release; A2P / caller SMS
- Force-push `main` or `staging`
- Real caller PII / live customer-number calls
- Opening `firestore.rules` (deny-all by design) or `database.rules.json`
- GitHub merge permission deny (paste the exact command)

Push to `main` does not deploy. Default-off merge ≠ activation.
